  "workflows": {},
  "implementation_policy": "Float64 CPU (Numba) solve of six independent clamped strip shells (discrete-shell membrane and bending with Kelvin-Voigt viscosity, strip self-contact) two-way coupled to planar rigid backpacks (x, z, pitch) that ride a kinematic belt and leave over a fixed lip, a stainless chute and a pickup deck whose planes are the solver's support profile; the bag collider is a signed-distance field of the scanned backpack (assets/scenes/metro_security_bag_curtain/backpack). Each whole-clip edit changes one edit_vocab parameter or presence flag through the shared DSL; the timed edit delete_curtain_at_frame_12 restores the exact float64 source state of frame 12 (t = 11/24 s) from the source states (simulate --source-cache), removes the curtain there and keeps solving, frames 1-11 being the source states. Motion and curtain deformation come only from the solver. The accepted native states of the source and the whole-clip edits are read from assets/scenes/metro_security_bag_curtain/native and the timed edit's merged states from the suite's inputs/native_timed/; they are replayed in Blender 4.3.2 (appearance/render_scene.py builds the scanner, belt, outfeed and station; appearance/realism.py is the current look; a timed DELETE hides the curtain from its edit frame) with a fixed camera; replay audits compare every frame with the states. tools/export_ground_truth.py writes per-frame ground truth from the same states, tools/publish_suite.py assembles a suite from render outputs, tools/encode_case.py encodes frames rendered on a host without ffmpeg and tools/worker_guard.py launches a Blender job on a checked idle GPU. Effective, uncalibrated material and friction values.",
